    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1989-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Inside the parentheses, \\(6 \\div 3 = 2.\\) Then multiplication comes before addition, so \\(9 \\times 2 = 18.\\)\n\nFinally, \\(-15 + 18 = 3.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D .",
      "hints": [
        "Follow the order of operations: parentheses first, then multiplication, then addition",
        "\\(6 \\div 3 = 2,\\) so the expression becomes \\(-15 + 9 \\times 2\\)"
      ],
